  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39838000",
      "title": "Building & Using a Reusable Input Component",
      "sourceHash": "4955319a22ae723ff285e11b7f520f58742c9cc3c70270a6d067a9d251e7ffcd",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 1.53,
          "en": "So now that you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.53,
          "end": 5.34,
          "en": "about different ways of handling forms submission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.34,
          "end": 7.5,
          "en": "and extracting user input values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.5,
          "end": 10.53,
          "en": "and of validating those values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.53,
          "end": 13.05,
          "en": "I wanna conclude this section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.05,
          "end": 18.05,
          "en": "by exploring some techniques of writing more reusable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.06,
          "end": 20.463,
          "en": "and easier to manage code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.42,
          "end": 25.62,
          "en": "And for that, I'm back here in the StateLogin.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.62,
          "end": 28.17,
          "en": "because it's in this component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.17,
          "end": 33.17,
          "en": "where I do have the most complex user input management.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.54,
          "end": 36.66,
          "en": "I'm keeping track of all the entered values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.66,
          "end": 39.3,
          "en": "upon every keystroke with state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.3,
          "end": 43.08,
          "en": "and I'm performing validation on every keystroke",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.08,
          "end": 46.023,
          "en": "and whenever input fields lose focus.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.76,
          "end": 51.84,
          "en": "And of course, that's not too bad in this component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.84,
          "end": 53.76,
          "en": "but keep in mind that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.76,
          "end": 58.76,
          "en": "we also have a relatively basic form, with only two inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60,
          "end": 65,
          "en": "And given that fact, we do indeed have quite some code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.13,
          "end": 67.8,
          "en": "And as you can also see here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.8,
          "end": 72.21000000000001,
          "en": "we also have quite a bit of code repetition here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.21000000000001,
          "end": 74.67,
          "en": "because in the end, we have the same logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.67,
          "end": 77.7,
          "en": "for both the email and the password field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.7,
          "end": 82.02,
          "en": "And we have the same JSX code down here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.02,
          "end": 87.02,
          "en": "just with some tiny details that are different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 87.21000000000001,
          "end": 88.995,
          "en": "For example, a different input type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.995,
          "end": 91.44,
          "en": "a different input name, and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.44,
          "end": 94.95,
          "en": "but the same general structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.95,
          "end": 99,
          "en": "And of course, whenever you have situations like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 99,
          "end": 103.71000000000001,
          "en": "where you have some kind of duplicate JSX code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.71000000000001,
          "end": 105.15,
          "en": "in this example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 105.15,
          "end": 108.81,
          "en": "you could consider building a custom component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 108.81,
          "end": 112.86,
          "en": "And that is indeed what I'll do here, therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.86,
          "end": 117.06,
          "en": "In the components folder, I'll add input.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 117.06,
          "end": 120.27,
          "en": "to build a custom input component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 120.27,
          "end": 123.78,
          "en": "which should in the end wrap this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 123.78,
          "end": 128.78,
          "en": "so that we can reuse this code easily, this JSX code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 130.71,
          "end": 132.556,
          "en": "So for that, in the input.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 132.556,
          "end": 136.803,
          "en": "I'll export a new function called Input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 138.06,
          "end": 143.06,
          "en": "and that function should return this JSX code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 143.94,
          "end": 144.813,
          "en": "in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 145.82999999999998,
          "end": 148.44,
          "en": "So this div with that label, the input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 148.44,
          "end": 153.44,
          "en": "and the error area below it, I'll output this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 156.36,
          "end": 159.93,
          "en": "But of course, we now have a lot of parts in this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 159.93,
          "end": 163.29,
          "en": "that should be configurable from outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 163.29,
          "end": 166.263,
          "en": "that should not be hard coded in this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 167.13,
          "end": 170.46,
          "en": "For example, the label text, but also the type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 170.46,
          "end": 172.563,
          "en": "the identifier, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 173.82,
          "end": 176.07,
          "en": "And therefore, we can start accepting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 176.07,
          "end": 178.413,
          "en": "and destructuring some props here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 179.52,
          "end": 181.62,
          "en": "For example, a label prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 181.62,
          "end": 184.533,
          "en": "which then can be used here instead of email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 186.96,
          "end": 189.81,
          "en": "But we also might want to get a name prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 189.81,
          "end": 192.903,
          "en": "which we can use as a value for name here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 194.64,
          "end": 197.4,
          "en": "Though we actually won't need this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 197.4,
          "end": 200.31,
          "en": "because instead, we can simply gather",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 200.31,
          "end": 205.14,
          "en": "all other extra props that might be set here on input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 205.14,
          "end": 208.353,
          "en": "and simply spread those onto the input field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 209.43,
          "end": 213.24,
          "en": "So that type and name can simply be set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 213.24,
          "end": 217.2,
          "en": "by setting type and name on our own input component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 217.2,
          "end": 220.1,
          "en": "And we then just forward these props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 220.1,
          "end": 222.393,
          "en": "to the input element we're wrapping.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 224.31,
          "end": 225.45,
          "en": "That being said,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 225.45,
          "end": 227.19,
          "en": "there still are some props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 227.19,
          "end": 231.96,
          "en": "which I wanna accept and destructure explicitly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 231.96,
          "end": 236.49,
          "en": "like this label prop, but also like the id prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 236.49,
          "end": 240.194,
          "en": "which could also be set and forwarded with that props object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 240.194,
          "end": 243.27,
          "en": "that gathers all remaining props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 243.27,
          "end": 246.27,
          "en": "but which I wanna pull out explicitly here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 246.27,
          "end": 249.57,
          "en": "since I don't just wanna set it on the input here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 249.57,
          "end": 254.283,
          "en": "but also on the label as a value for HTML 4.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 255.6,
          "end": 258.87,
          "en": "In addition, things can of course go wrong,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 258.87,
          "end": 263.4,
          "en": "and therefore, I also want to get an error prop here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 263.4,
          "end": 267.693,
          "en": "which I use to show an error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 268.59,
          "end": 270.87,
          "en": "So I'm using it to find out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 270.87,
          "end": 273.63,
          "en": "whether an error message should be shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 273.63,
          "end": 278.493,
          "en": "and I expect it to that error message if we should show one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 279.36,
          "end": 283.05,
          "en": "so that I'm using it both for this conditional check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 283.05,
          "end": 286.023,
          "en": "and as a value that then being output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 287.1,
          "end": 289.08299999999997,
          "en": "Now when it comes to onBlur, onChange,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 290.04,
          "end": 295.04,
          "en": "and the value prop here, we can get rid of the value prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 296.01,
          "end": 299.04,
          "en": "and set that through the remaining props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 299.04,
          "end": 301.683,
          "en": "that are spread onto this element anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 302.7,
          "end": 307.41,
          "en": "And I can do the same here for onBlur and onChange",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 307.41,
          "end": 311.103,
          "en": "to make this input as reusable as possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 312.6,
          "end": 315.54,
          "en": "And with that, we got some pretty lean code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 315.54,
          "end": 319.56,
          "en": "And back in StateLogin.jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 319.56,
          "end": 322.5,
          "en": "we can now use this input element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 322.5,
          "end": 326.703,
          "en": "here directly in this control-row div in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 328.89,
          "end": 333.89,
          "en": "by, first of all, importing it from the input.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 336.6,
          "end": 339.993,
          "en": "and by then using it here and setting some props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 341.25,
          "end": 345.15,
          "en": "For example, the label prop here should be set to email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 345.15,
          "end": 347.56,
          "en": "So to this text which I wanna output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 348.42,
          "end": 351.243,
          "en": "because we'll soon remove this div here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 352.77,
          "end": 355.14300000000003,
          "en": "The id prop should be set to email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 356.13,
          "end": 358.65,
          "en": "the type prop should be set to email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 358.65,
          "end": 361.92,
          "en": "and the name should also be set to email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 361.92,
          "end": 365.49,
          "en": "And type and name are, for example, props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 365.49,
          "end": 368.7,
          "en": "that will be set on the input element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 368.7,
          "end": 370.38,
          "en": "inside of the input component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 370.38,
          "end": 373.3,
          "en": "with help of these forwarded props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 374.67,
          "end": 378.33,
          "en": "I'm not explicitly pulling out type and name here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 378.33,
          "end": 381.93,
          "en": "Instead, I'm just gathering and spreading remaining props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 381.93,
          "end": 384.6,
          "en": "and that's how type and name will end up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 384.6,
          "end": 388.053,
          "en": "on that wrapped input in my own input component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 390.45,
          "end": 394.53,
          "en": "Now, I will also forward onBlur, onChange, and value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 394.53,
          "end": 398.193,
          "en": "and therefore, copy those props from down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 399.3,
          "end": 403.77,
          "en": "And with that, we can get rid of that div down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 403.77,
          "end": 405.84000000000003,
          "en": "And therefore, we were able to get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 405.84000000000003,
          "end": 409.683,
          "en": "of a bunch of JSX code by using this custom component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 411,
          "end": 413.58,
          "en": "And we can now reuse that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 413.58,
          "end": 416.373,
          "en": "to all the output and input for the password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 417.96,
          "end": 422.96,
          "en": "where the label is password, the id is password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 423.12,
          "end": 427.863,
          "en": "the type is password, and the name is password, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 430.02,
          "end": 433.2,
          "en": "And for onBlur, onChange, and value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 433.2,
          "end": 436.05,
          "en": "I can again copy the code from down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 436.05,
          "end": 439.77,
          "en": "though here I don't even have an onBlur listener yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 439.77,
          "end": 441.813,
          "en": "which I'll change now though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 442.77,
          "end": 444.91,
          "en": "So here I'll now call handleInputBlur",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 447.37,
          "end": 449.523,
          "en": "and blur the password input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 451.53,
          "end": 454.773,
          "en": "just as I'm also doing it for the email here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 456.57,
          "end": 459.21,
          "en": "And with that, we can also get rid of this div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 459.21,
          "end": 461.094,
          "en": "and we now simplified this form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 461.094,
          "end": 464.193,
          "en": "by using our own custom component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 465.57,
          "end": 469.40999999999997,
          "en": "Now I removed one div closing tag too much,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 469.40999999999997,
          "end": 470.85,
          "en": "so let me re add this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 470.85,
          "end": 474.33,
          "en": "And with that, the JSX code just got leaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 474.33,
          "end": 477.63,
          "en": "And if we save that and go to the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 477.63,
          "end": 482.63,
          "en": "to import this login component from /components/StateLogin,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 486.33,
          "end": 489.453,
          "en": "you will see that it will work Just as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 490.62,
          "end": 493.86,
          "en": "The only remaining thing we have to do for this to work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 493.86,
          "end": 497.46,
          "en": "back in StateLogin.jsx is, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 497.46,
          "end": 501.45,
          "en": "to find out whether those inputs are valid or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 501.45,
          "end": 504.66,
          "en": "which we're already doing here with emailIsInvalid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
